@* A disabled button fires no pointer events, so a tooltip on it never opens — which is the one
   moment a reader most needs to be told why. Wrap it: the span takes the hover, the button
   stays disabled, and the reason is announced because the wrapper is focusable. *@
<span tabindex="0" data-slot="tooltip-trigger" data-target="tip-why"
      aria-describedby="tip-why" class="inline-block w-fit">
    <Button Variant="outline" disabled>Disabled</Button>
</span>
<TooltipContent Id="tip-why">This feature is currently unavailable</TooltipContent>
